Sentence 1: In common with most carnivorous plants, they grow in moist soils which are poor in dissolved minerals, where their carnivorous nature gives them a competitive advantage; terrestrial varieties of "Utricularia" can frequently be found alongside representatives of the carnivorous genera–"Sarracenia", "Drosera" and others–in very wet areas where continuously moving water removes most soluble minerals from the soil.
Utricularia species.
